# rule.always.boot-an-oversized-subdomain-as-its-catalog

> **when an enbriefed subdomain is too large to boot whole, boot its CATALOG at `say` and list every
> member under `not`. each member stays reffable via a path the catalog lets a reader compute.**

```yaml
say:
  - briefs/domain.terms/catalog.of=term._.md     # every name + the path formula
not:
  - briefs/domain.terms/term=*.md                # members: read on demand, never booted
```

## .why

a `ref` entry boots its **path** — so a subdomain at `ref` charges one line per member to every
session, forever, and the charge grows with each member. `ref` caps a body's cost, never a count's.
a catalog names every member at a fraction of that, since the path is computed, not printed.

**the `not` is load-critical**: an unlisted member falls back into `<also>` and costs its path
anyway. a catalog with no `not` beside it pays twice.

## .the test

> **would a reader rather see every member's path, or one index that names them all?**

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| a boot spec globs ~20+ files of one subdomain | the strongest cue. catalog it |
| `rhx cost` ranks `<briefs.ref>` or `<also>` near the top | the path list is the cost |
| a boot spec runs over budget | cut paths before cues — they are the cheapest tokens |
| a subdomain begins to fill a directory | write its catalog at the second member, not the fiftieth |
| members are named by coordinate (`term=$name`) | state the path formula once |

the catalog owes: every member by name, grouped by boundary root · the path formula, once, with an
example · a census note (hand-kept; a member on disk absent here is drift) · its rules by path.
it obeys `rule.require.catalog-is-an-index`.

measured 2026-10-16, this repo's `role=any` boot: 148 glossary terms at `ref` cost ~5.3k tokens of
paths per boot; one catalog at `say` (934) plus a `not` brought 29.8k → 23.9k, every term one
computed path away.

blocker: a catalog at `say` whose members are left out of `not`.
nitpick: a catalogable subdomain of ~20+ members booted as paths · a catalog that prints every path
where one formula would compute it.
false positive: a handful of files at `ref` · a subdomain every boot needs whole.

⇒ see also: `rule.require.catalog-is-an-index` · `rule.prefer.rules-that-refout` ·
`rule.forbid.itemization-without-coordinates` · `rule.require.summary-at-the-cluster-root`.
